Blackdrift: never send Glean telemetry or the daily usage ping.

Why: Blackdrift does not report anything to Mozilla. Upstream Focus already keeps
general Glean collection off (isTelemetryEnabled() returns false), but the
daily usage ping is on by default in focusRelease and its two pings
(usage-reporting, usage-deletion-request) set follows_collection_enabled:
false, so they upload even when Glean upload is disabled. This patch:

- passes uploadEnabled = false to Glean.initialize directly, so a future
  upstream change to isTelemetryEnabled() cannot turn upload back on;
- turns both usage pings off in GleanUsageReporting.setEnabled(), whatever
  the caller asks for, so nothing is sent even if the stored preference is
  true;
- makes the daily usage ping preference default to false;
- removes the "Data Choices" category from Privacy & Security settings,
  because a switch that can no longer send anything would mislead users;
- drops the androidTest robot's checks of that switch
  (SettingsPrivacyMenuRobot.verifyPrivacySettingsItems), which would fail
  now that it is gone;
- points the Privacy & Security summary ("Tracking, cookies, data choices")
  at a new non-translatable blackdrift_privacy_and_security_summary in a new
  values/blackdrift_telemetry_strings.xml. No translated string without "data
  choices" fits, and overriding the upstream key would only change English.

Glean still runs locally because other components record metrics through
it; with upload off nothing leaves the device.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

